  "approximations": [
    "Board outline: KiCad Edge.Cuts, arcs tessellated at 6 degrees (max chord error ~0.003 mm for the 1 mm arcs). Outline and window are exact to that; the 1.6 mm thickness is the stackup.",
    "NPTH slots are drawn as stadiums from the json sizes with KiCad's absolute pad angle (the scad D_SLOTS lists the 1 x 2.5 slots rotated 90 degrees the other way).",
    "SoM: a 50 x 40 x 1.6 mm PCB at 6.5 mm and a 2.5 mm parts-envelope block (not the real FPGA and regulator shapes). Mass model: one uniform 50 x 40 x 4.1 mm box.",
    "Components (B2B connectors, flow sensor, ToF, IMU, USB-C, JTAG, ESP32, switches, motor connectors, inductor): courtyard-sized boxes with datasheet heights; USB-C is an 8.94 x 7.65 mm box.",
    "Clip-on arms: hull of a 6 mm circle at the rail end and a 9 mm collar at the motor, 4 mm thick from z = -3 mm. Placeholder.",
    "Motors: 7 x 20 mm cylinders with a 1 mm shaft stub. Props: two-blade planform with 12 degree pitch inside a 51 mm disc; a visual stand-in, not the HQ blade.",
    "Camera: box bracket 3 x 8 x 3.4 mm plus a 3 mm lens stub; the real flex module and bracket are not in the PCB.",
    "Battery and holder: boxes. The 20 mm battery width equals the window width.",
    "Colliders: boxes and cylinders on the same inferred heights; the resting pose depends on the assumed motor can bottom (-3 mm) and the inferred connector heights.",
    "Mass: the populated-board mass (17.6 g less the 8.2 g bare board = 9.4 g) is spread over a 51 x 40 x 3.8 mm box; antenna, camera bracket and battery plug are not placed separately.",
    "Antenna pigtail, wires, ToF breakouts (unfitted slots), standoffs and fasteners are not modelled; their mass is inside the weight-note figures or unknown."
  ],
  "assumptions_affecting_dynamics": [
    "Mass 58.5 g is the sum of the weight-note parts; the note's own check gives 58.1 g; the real flight-ready weight is unmeasured.",
    "CoM z = 3.9 mm above the board top depends on the SoM box (z 6.5-10.6), the battery (z -2.4 to 4.6, centred x = y = 0) and the motor assemblies (centre z = 7 mm). Battery x/y position moves the CoM 0.18 mm per mm of shift.",
    "Inertia comes from uniform boxes and cylinders. Izz is set mainly by the four 3.3 g rotor masses at 46 mm; Ixx and Iyy by the same plus the stack height. The mass split inside a rotor (can, arm, prop) is unknown; a prop-heavy split (centre z = 12 mm) changes Ixx and Iyy by about +3 percent.",
    "Rotor plane z = 18.5 mm and can bottom z = -3 mm are assumptions; they set where the rotors sit relative to the CoM (about 15 mm above it) and the can contact height.",
    "Spin signs are copied from dronesim and unverified; they set the sign of the yaw reaction torque of each motor.",
    "Prop diameter 51 mm (user-confirmed) is used; the PCB prop circles say 47 mm.",
    "Thrust, drag, ground effect, battery and motor dynamics are not part of this asset."
  ],
